                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Randomly came across this. Never heard of it. Took a quick glance at the preview and the reviews. I was curious. Even more when I seen it was on sale for pocket change. \r\n\r\nKind of reminds Me of back when there would be interactive DVD's. I didn't know what to expect. After roughly 5 hours of gameplay. Worth it. \r\n\r\nHumorously, even though the game is as old as Me. And I'm as old as some of the characters in it, as they were then...It still holds up. The story takes you for a roller coaster ride. It takes awhile, but before you know it, things get REAL, real quick. Even that's an understatement. \r\n\r\nThe soundtrack is cool, and with it, the scenery. (I could make a few jokes) The Nostalgia is nice. The Characters are well put together. The acting in the cutscenes can be touch and go, but some parts hit you. One part actually made me tear up a bit, which is rare. Some things are a little cheesy. What do you expect from 1998? BUT, it's still relevant to today. Just, minus- the fashion and the cars. And smartphones haha.\r\n\r\nRegardless of any hiccups, It's certainly a brain teaser. And it gets you hooked. Almost exactly like when you watch a good film and you can't wait to see what happens in the end. Very much recommended! Even more so when it's on sale. One of the best \"on the whim\" decisions I ever made was to get it. \r\n\r\n",
